new framework for spatial-temporal network data forecasting"},{"key":"ref14","article-title":"Graph wavenet for deep spatial-temporal graph modeling","author":"Z Wu","year":"2019","journal-title":"IJCAI"},{"key":"ref15","author":"C Shang","year":"2021","journal-title":"Discrete graph structure learning for forecasting multiple time series"},{"key":"ref16","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"238","DOI":"10.1109\/TNNLS.2016.2574963","article-title":"Laplacian echo state network for multivariate time series prediction","volume":"29","author":"M Han","year":"2017","journal-title":"IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems"},{"key":"ref17","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"37","DOI":"10.1007\/978-3-642-24797-2_4","author":"A Graves","year":"2012","journal-title":"Long short-term memory, Supervised sequence labelling with recurrent neural networks"},{"key":"ref18","volume":"27","author":"I Sutskever","year":"2014","journal-title":"Sequence to sequence learning with neural networks"},{"key":"ref19","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"4","DOI":"10.1109\/TNNLS.2020.2978386","article-title":"A comprehensive survey on graph neural networks","volume":"32","author":"Z Wu","year":"2020","journal-title":"IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems"},{"key":"ref20","author":"Y Li","year":"2018","journal-title":"Diffusion convolutional recurrent neural network: Data-driven traffic forecasting"},{"key":"ref21","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"3848","DOI":"10.1109\/TITS.2019.2935152","article-title":"Tgcn: A temporal graph convolutional network for traffic prediction","volume":"21","author":"L Zhao","year":"2019","journal-title":"IEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems"},{"key":"ref22","first-page":"2733","article-title":"Decoupled dynamic spatial-temporal graph neural network for traffic forecasting","volume":"15","author":"Z Shao","year":"2022","journal-title":"VLDB"},{"key":"ref23","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","DOI":"10.1016\/j.patcog.2023.109670","article-title":"A decomposition dynamic graph convolutional recurrent network for traffic forecasting","volume":"142","author":"W Weng","year":"2023","journal-title":"Pattern Recognition"},{"key":"ref24","article-title":"Dynamic graph structure learning for multivariate time series forecasting","volume":"138","author":"Z L Li","year":"2023","journal-title":"Pattern Recognition"},{"key":"ref25","volume":"1","author":"Z Wang","year":"2015","journal-title":"Encoding time series as images for visual inspection and classification using tiled convolutional neural networks"},{"key":"ref26","first-page":"95","article-title":"Modeling long-and short-term temporal patterns with deep neural networks","author":"G Lai","year":"2018","journal-title":"ACM SIGIR"},{"key":"ref27","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"96","DOI":"10.3141\/1748-12","article-title":"Freeway performance measurement system: mining loop detector data","volume":"1748","author":"C Chen","year":"2001","journal-title":"Transportation Research Record"},{"key":"ref28","author":"F Yu","year":"2016","journal-title":"Multi-scale context aggregation by dilated convolutions"},{"key":"ref29","first-page":"22419","article-title":"Autoformer: Decomposition transformers with auto-correlation for long-term series forecasting","volume":"34","author":"H Wu","year":"2021","journal-title":"NeurIPS"},{"key":"ref30","author":"M Xu","year":"2020","journal-title":"Spatialtemporal transformer networks for traffic flow forecasting"},{"key":"ref31","first-page":"1684","author":"Y Chen","year":"2021","journal-title":"Z-gcnets: Time zigzags at graph convolutional networks for time series forecasting"},{"key":"ref32","first-page":"17804","volume":"33","author":"L Bai","year":"2020","journal-title":"Adaptive graph convolutional recurrent network for traffic forecasting"},{"key":"ref33","first-page":"6367","volume":"36","author":"J Choi","year":"2022","journal-title":"Graph neural controlled differential equations for traffic forecasting"},{"key":"ref34","author":"E Jang","year":"2017","journal-title":"Categorical reparameterization with gumbelsoftmax"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,6,21]],"date-time":"2024-06-21T14:26:11Z","timestamp":1718979971000},"score":28.402836,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=4872537"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"references-count":34,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.4872537","published":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,25]],"date-time":"2026-06-25T16:45:53Z","timestamp":1782405953302,"version":"3.54.5"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"group-title":"SSRN","reference-count":28,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>Short-term footfall forecasting is important for staffing, crowd management, energy scheduling, and event-aware operations in large commercial areas. However, this task remains challenging because pedestrian flow is affected by heterogeneous external factors, strong periodic patterns, and abrupt local deviations. Existing forecasting methods often struggle to jointly model multimodal signals and maintain interpretability under high-frequency prediction settings. To address these challenges, this paper proposes MFF-LLM, a multimodal LLM-based forecasting framework with an offline\u2013online design. In the offline stage, aligned observations are transformed into modality-specific token streams. In the online stage, these tokens are processed by a dual-path forecasting network that integrates Stage-1 fusion, a frozen Transformer backbone, explicit modality posterior estimation, history-guided routing, and a two-stage prediction head. Experiments on real-world footfall forecasting show that the MFF-LLM family achieves the strongest and most consistent MAE performance across multiple forecast horizons. Further ablation and mechanism analyses show that the seasonal prior, explicit modality branch, and structured multimodal fusion are key contributors to the final performance. Case studies also demonstrate that the proposed model can follow event-day deviations, preserve major peak\u2013valley patterns, and capture short-term dynamic changes with reasonable fidelity. These results indicate that MFF-LLM provides an effective and interpretable solution for short-term multimodal footfall forecasting.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.6996730","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,25]],"date-time":"2026-06-25T15:41:31Z","timestamp":1782402091000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["A Multimodal LLM Framework for Short-Term Footfall Time Series Forecasting"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-4362-5652","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Zhijie","family":"Li","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0000-1013-5724","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Gao","family":"Libo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Wang","family":"Fuqi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Changhua","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"78","reference":[{"key":"ref1","author":"Al Sahili","year":"2023","journal-title":"Spatio-temporal graph neural networks: A survey"},{"key":"ref2","first-page":"7320","article-title":"N-hits: Neural hierarchical interpolation for time series forecasting","author":"C Challu","year":"2023","journal-title":"AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence"},{"key":"ref3","author":"J Chen","year":"2025","journal-title":"Decoupling spatio-temporal prediction: When lightweight large models meet adaptive hypergraphs"},{"key":"ref4","article-title":"Granger-tsllm: Granger causality enhanced llms with residual-quantized tokenizer for multivariate time series forecasting","volume":"196","author":"J Chu","year":"2026","journal-title":"Neural Networks"},{"key":"ref5","article-title":"Lcmf: A llm-enhanced cross-modal fusion framework for universal temporal forecasting","volume":"341","author":"S Du","year":"2026","journal-title":"Knowledge-Based Systems"},{"key":"ref6","article-title":"Fm-llm: A frequency-enhanced mixture-of-experts framework for adapting llms to time series forecasting","volume":"341","author":"R Gu","year":"2026","journal-title":"Knowledge-Based Systems"},{"key":"ref7","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"5388","DOI":"10.1109\/TKDE.2023.3333824","article-title":"2024a. Spatio-temporal graph neural networks for predictive learning in urban computing: A survey","volume":"36","author":"G Jin","journal-title":"IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering"},{"key":"ref8","author":"M Jin","year":"2024","journal-title":"Time-LLM: Time series forecasting by reprogramming large language models"},{"key":"ref9","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","DOI":"10.1016\/j.eswa.2023.120281","article-title":"Spatio-temporal graph mixformer for traffic forecasting","volume":"228","author":"M Lablack","year":"2023","journal-title":"Expert Systems With Applications"},{"key":"ref10","first-page":"18780","article-title":"2025a. Timecma: Towards llm-empowered multivariate time series forecasting via cross-modality alignment","author":"C Liu","journal-title":"Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence"},{"key":"ref11","article-title":"Spatial-temporal large language model for traffic prediction","author":"C Liu","year":"2024","journal-title":"Proceedings of the 25th IEEE International Conference on Mobile Data Management (MDM)"},{"key":"ref12","article-title":"Towards cross-modality modeling for time series analytics: A survey in the llm era","author":"C Liu","year":"2025","journal-title":"Proceedings of the 34th Inter